WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.500
India is South Asia's vast peninsula, home to the ancient Indus Valley Civilization.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:11.000
The majestic Himalayan range forms the northern boundary, crowned by Kangchenjunga at 8,586 meters.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:17.000
In Agra, the Taj Mahal stands as a world-famous ivory-white marble mausoleum on the Yamuna river.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:23.000
The elegant Saree is woven with Banarasi silk and gold Zari embroidery dating back centuries.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:29.000
Classical Indian music resonates through the multi-stringed Sitar and rhythmic Tabla drums.

